  "content": {
    "id": "p48-q17-24-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "17",
    "prompt": "Solve for $0^\\circ\\le x\\le360^\\circ$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p48-q17-24-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$$\\frac{\\tan3x-\\tan2x}{1+\\tan3x\\tan2x}=-1$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p48-q17-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "No solution.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p48-q17-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The tangent difference identity gives candidates ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "135^\\circ,315^\\circ",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", but both make ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\tan2x",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " undefined.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "For values where the original expression is defined, use the tangent difference identity.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan(3x-2x)&=-1\\\\\\tan x&=-1\\\\x&=135^\\circ,315^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nAt $x=135^\\circ$, $\\tan2x=\\tan270^\\circ$ is undefined. At $x=315^\\circ$, $\\tan2x=\\tan630^\\circ$ is also undefined. Neither candidate satisfies the original equation, so there is no solution.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 92
      },
      {
        "id": "p48-q17-24-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\cos2x=1+\\sin x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=0^\\circ,180^\\circ,210^\\circ,330^\\circ,360^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}1-2\\sin^2x&=1+\\sin x\\\\2\\sin^2x+\\sin x&=0\\\\\\sin x(2\\sin x+1)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nKeep both factor branches.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin x&=0\\quad\\text{or}\\quad\\sin x=-\\frac12\\\\x&=0^\\circ,180^\\circ,210^\\circ,330^\\circ,360^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p48-q17-24-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$3\\cos2x+5\\sin x=4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p48-q19-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "x=\\sin^{-1}\\!\\left(\\frac13\\right),30^\\circ,150^\\circ,180^\\circ-\\sin^{-1}\\!\\left(\\frac13\\right)",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p48-q19-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\cos2x=1-2\\sin^2x",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and factor the quadratic in ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\sin x",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}3(1-2\\sin^2x)+5\\sin x&=4\\\\3-6\\sin^2x+5\\sin x&=4\\\\6\\sin^2x-5\\sin x+1&=0\\\\(3\\sin x-1)(2\\sin x-1)&=0\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin x&=\\frac13\\quad\\text{or}\\quad\\sin x=\\frac12\\end{align*}$$\nFor $\\sin x=\\frac13$,\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\sin^{-1}\\!\\left(\\frac13\\right),\\ 180^\\circ-\\sin^{-1}\\!\\left(\\frac13\\right).\\end{align*}$$\nFor $\\sin x=\\frac12$,\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=30^\\circ,150^\\circ.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 80
      },
      {
        "id": "p48-q17-24-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\tan2x\\tan x=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=30^\\circ,150^\\circ,210^\\circ,330^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "Let $t=\\tan x$ and use the tangent double-angle identity.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{2t}{1-t^2}\\,t&=1\\\\2t^2&=1-t^2\\\\3t^2&=1\\\\t&=\\pm\\frac1{\\sqrt{3}}\\\\\\tan x&=\\pm\\frac1{\\sqrt{3}}\\\\x&=30^\\circ,150^\\circ,210^\\circ,330^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nBoth $\\tan x$ and $\\tan2x$ are defined at all four values, which satisfy the original equation.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 94
      },
      {
        "id": "p48-q17-24-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$3(1-\\sin x)=1+\\cos2x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=30^\\circ,90^\\circ,150^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}3(1-\\sin x)&=1+(1-2\\sin^2x)\\\\3-3\\sin x&=2-2\\sin^2x\\\\2\\sin^2x-3\\sin x+1&=0\\\\(2\\sin x-1)(\\sin x-1)&=0\\\\\\sin x&=\\frac12\\quad\\text{or}\\quad\\sin x=1\\\\x&=30^\\circ,90^\\circ,150^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p48-q17-24-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\cos x\\sin2x-\\sin x\\cos2x=\\frac12$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=30^\\circ,150^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "Use the sine difference identity in reverse.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin(2x-x)&=\\frac12\\\\\\sin x&=\\frac12\\\\x&=30^\\circ,150^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p48-q17-24-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$\\cos x\\cos3x+\\sin3x\\sin x=-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=90^\\circ,270^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "Use the cosine difference identity in reverse.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos(3x-x)&=-1\\\\\\cos2x&=-1\\\\2x&=180^\\circ,540^\\circ\\\\x&=90^\\circ,270^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p48-q17-24-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$\\cos(x+60^\\circ)=\\cos(x)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=150^\\circ,330^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "Expand and collect terms.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos x\\cos60^\\circ-\\sin x\\sin60^\\circ&=\\cos x\\\\\\frac12\\cos x-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}2\\sin x&=\\cos x\\\\-\\sqrt{3}\\sin x&=\\cos x\\end{align*}$$\nIf $\\cos x=0$, the equation is not satisfied. Divide by $\\cos x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan x&=-\\frac1{\\sqrt{3}}\\\\x&=150^\\circ,330^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 70
      }
    ]
  },
